# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""R1 automatic DIST-only TD calibration, v1.8 ADAPTIVE FINE 512-node IDP CDF SILENT.

Run ONCE from Visum > Scripts > Execute script file, not from Procedure Sequence.
Adapted control pattern: user's 15A9 V3/V3.22 (apply, native execute, evaluate,
accept/reject, rollback and continue). Objective: full 512-point IDP cumulative distribution curves + mean distance.

Does not run TG/assignment/14A/14B, change P/A or network impedances, refit LONG
mixture, create another Visum, or call LoadVersion. Only native TD is executed.
Patched M9001/M9697 target cells are verified before any model writes.
Result matrices are cleared before native TD (same purpose as TD's reset option)
and restored from exact snapshots on rejection/failure. They are NEVER fitted by
cell correction. FOREIGN is removed temporarily from TD's DSTRATSET.

No external CSV, 11D helper, scipy or environment variables are required.
NumPy is required. All 512-point original IDP DIST_KM curves (plus 12b frozen LONG mixture) are embedded.
Six-bin/ten-bin histograms remain diagnostics only, not the primary loss.
All Python progress/error messages are FILE ONLY, with no Python print() calls.
Default evidence/checkpoints are written to LOCALAPPDATA, not the script
folder (which can be OneDrive-synced and intermittently lock JSON files).
Native non-critical procedure warnings are suppressed using the documented
Visum 2026 GUI user preference, restored after the run. Critical native errors
are NOT acknowledged automatically. The run fails closed if silent preference
cannot be verified via COM before any model mutation.
A .ver backup is saved to a NEW run directory; original files are not overwritten.
This is a distribution-only checkpoint: downstream vehicle matrices/assignment
are NOT updated. Finalization of those stages is deliberately outside this loop.
"""
